{"repositoryId":512835706,"availability":"available","full":"hyperledger-identus/cloud-agent","name":"cloud-agent","description":"Identus Cloud Agent","category":"Other","language":"Scala","stars":96,"forks":34,"created":"2022-07-11T16:42:39Z","updated":"2026-10-15T08:04:45Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://identus.io/","topics":["identus","scala","ssi"],"demo":"https://hyperledger-identus.github.io/docs/home/quick-start","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:23:29.999Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T08:23:29.999Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T08:23:29.999Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T08:23:29.999Z","stars":96,"forks":34}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Cloud Agent is a W3C/Aries standards-based cloud agent written in Scala that provides self-sovereign identity services to build products and solutions based on it. The term \"cloud\" indicates that it operates on servers and is not intended for use on mobile devices.","Cloud Agent supports standard-based protocols built on top of DIDComm V2 for issuing, verifying, and holding verifiable credentials using both JWT and Hyperledger AnonCreds (coming soon) formats.","In order to use the Cloud Agent, you establish a business logic controller responsible for communicating with the agent (initiating HTTP requests and processing webhook notifications). This controller can be created using any programming language capable of sending and receiving HTTP requests."],"features":["W3C-compliant did:prism and did:peer methods","HTTP events notification","Cardano as a distributed ledger","Secrets management with Hashicorp vault"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hyperledger-identus/cloud-agent/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1bb96579680f65987d5c3f7388bcf582fe5f776c63afd6b2bf2e8a72e6fafbd7","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T08:23:30.256Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T08:23:30.256Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"T